<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minusinsk Basin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Minusinsk Basin is a lowland on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-river">Yenisei River</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, ringed by the Sayan and Kuznetsk Alatau mountains, today in Khakassia and Krasnoyarsk Krai, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Its fertile steppe was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> cultures such as the Afanasievo, Karasuk and Tagar, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-kyrgyz">Yenisei Kyrgyz</a>, whose runic inscriptions survive there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minusinsk-basin.jpg" alt="Minusinsk Basin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dmitry_Hertz · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yenisey_river_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
